## Why This Is Asked

Tests a real-world asynchronous export flow requiring idempotency, retry logic, and observability. It validates high-concurrency behavior and failure modes across the message broker and downstream analytics partner.

## Key Concepts

- Idempotent POST endpoints with deduplication keys
- At-least-once vs exactly-once processing semantics
- End-to-end observability and monitoring
- Exponential backoff retry strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example test skeleton for idempotent export
async function testIdempotentExport(exportId) {
  const res1 = await post('/exports', {
    user_id: 'user123',
    export_options: { format: 'csv', date_range: '30d' },
    export_id: exportId
  });

  const res2 = await post('/exports', {
    user_id: 'user123',
    export_options: { format: 'csv', date_range: '30d' },
    export_id: exportId
  });

  // First request should queue the export
  assert(res1.status === 202);
  // Second request should return existing export
  assert(res2.status === 200 && res2.data.export_id === exportId);
}
```
